Ember Throne credits

Characters: built from CC0 bases by this repository's own tools
  sources     Quaternius, "Universal Base Characters" (Standard, free) and "Modular Character Outfits - Fantasy"
              (Standard, free), CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication):
                https://quaternius.com/packs/universalbasecharacters.html
                https://quaternius.com/packs/modularcharacteroutfitsfantasy.html
                https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
              The files used (the ranger and peasant outfits, the two base bodies' heads, eyes and brows, the hair
              styles), with their textures resized, are in tools/chars/cc0 with the packs' licence notes
              (LICENSE-base.txt, LICENSE-outfits.txt). CC0 asks for nothing; the credit is given anyway.
  changes     tools/chars/blender/build_chars.py, cast.py, dress.py (run headless in Blender; Blender is a tool, its
              output is ours): each figure posed to the game's rest, sized and bulked, its head and hands enlarged,
              recoloured, its skin baked into one atlas; the plate, helmets, crowns, horns, robes, coats, capes, masks
              and bracers are generated there. tools/chars/make-characters.mjs (copied from more-cartwheel-examples'
              brawler, with this game's clips: the sword combo, the heavy spin, the dive roll, the sidesteps, the
              kneel at a shrine, the flask, the push, the roar) puts them on the game's skeleton with its clips.
              tools/chars/build-cast.sh runs both.

Everything else in this game is generated by this repository's own code:
  world       world.c (the terrain's heights and paint, every building, stair, gate and door, all from tables at
              start-up) and tools/make-world-assets.mjs (the terrain layers, the building textures and every prop:
              weapons, keys, the heart vessel, chests, shrines, trees, rocks, braziers, pillars, banners)
  sound       fx.c and main.c (every sound and the music are computed)
  fonts       the engine's built-in UI font (see the engine's NOTICE)
  art         tools/capture-art.sh and tools/make-art.mjs (the launcher art from the game's own frames; the name set in
              DejaVu Serif Bold, the system's free font, Bitstream Vera licence)

Third-party assets: the CC0 character sources above; the launcher art's lettering uses the DejaVu Serif Bold font.
